# COSMIC-specific removals (appended to config/remove.list; same format).
#
# cosmic-session hard-requires them, but larch ships no terminal (software
# comes from Sawmill), and users are managed only from the boot menu (Manage
# LARCH → Manage users), so no first-run setup wizard.
cosmic-term
cosmic-initial-setup

# cosmic-greeter requires greetd-selinux, which pulls in the whole SELinux
# policy and its tools. larch runs without SELinux, and with no
# /etc/selinux/config at all (scripts/setup-chroot.sh: SELINUX=disabled makes
# systemd hit the kernel's removed runtime-disable switch);
# remove-files.list deletes what the policy left behind.
greetd-selinux
selinux-policy*
policycoreutils*
python3-policycoreutils
libselinux-utils
